.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Hund and Mulliken&#x27;s molecular-orbital theory builds one-electron orbitals spread over the whole molecule as a linear combination of atomic orbitals, \psi_\pm=c_A\chi_A\pm c_B\chi_B. H2PlusVariational does this for H2+ with one Gaussian orbital per proton: diagonalizing the 2x2 problem gives the in-phase bonding orbital (equal coefficients, energy below the isolated-atom level) and the out-of-phase antibonding orbital (opposite coefficients, energy above it). Following both orbital energies from short bond lengths out to separated atoms gives Mulliken&#x27;s correlation diagram for the simplest molecule.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/quantum/hartree_fock/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_lcao_molecular_orbitals_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/quantum/hartree_fock/plot_01_lcao_molecular_orbitals`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Hund-Mulliken LCAO molecular orbitals of H2+: bonding and antibonding</div>
    </div>


